{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from two incredible weeks in Japan, and my head is still spinning with vibrant sights, delicious food, and fascinating culture! From the moment I stepped off the plane in Tokyo, I was captivated.\n\nTokyo was a whirlwind of neon lights, bustling crowds, and incredible food. I spent days exploring Shibuya crossing (a must-see!), getting lost in the quirky shops of Harajuku, and indulging in ramen at every opportunity. The sensory overload was exhilarating!\n\nNext, I took the shinkansen (bullet train) to Kyoto, a completely different experience. Here, ancient temples and serene gardens replaced the city's energy. I wandered through Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates, and found peace in the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.  A traditional tea ceremony was a highlight – so calming and graceful.\n\nThe food, oh the food! Sushi, ramen, tempura, okonomiyaki… I tried it all, and everything was exquisite.  Don't be afraid to venture beyond the tourist spots; some of the best meals were in small, local restaurants.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions seamlessly blending with modern innovation. It’s a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you wanting more. I can’t wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0009869233472272754}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.17473071813583374}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0010996968485414982}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268293976783752}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.06704318523406982}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.23437008261680603}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.8984939455986023}, {"token": "▁back", "logprob": -0.04315086081624031}, {"token": "▁from", "logp